Chapter: CryptoBigTest
  cites Foreword chapter CryptoBig
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Modular exponentiation, checked against an independent implementation.

 The vectors come from .NET's System.Numerics.BigInteger over a real
 2048-bit RSA modulus minted by openssl. That matters more than the
 arithmetic being hard: a bignum tested only against itself is the
 compression stack's mistake in another costume, and the whole point of
 this chapter is to eventually believe what a stranger's certificate
 says.

 We say:

